  <floater.string name="whats_in">A report goes to the Alchemy developers' Sentry project, the one crash reports go to, and only when you press Send.

Every report carries:
- your message, and your email if you give one
- the viewer's version, channel and build
- your operating system and graphics card
- where the viewer was in starting up or running, and the region you were in (unless an RLVa restriction hides your location)
- whether crash reports are on, and an id for this run of the viewer, so a report can be matched to a crash from the same run

With "Include my avatar name", your avatar's name and key go too, so a developer can find you in world. Without it, your name and key are hidden in the logs, but logs and system information can still say things about you: untick them as well for a report that says nothing about who you are.

Each attachment you tick goes as you see it in View, as it is when you press Send. Logs go as their last 4 MB, with the addresses that act for your session hidden; while RLVa hides your location, they stay out. Settings you've changed leave out keys, passwords, tokens and email addresses, and text that could name you, a file or a place reads as hidden.

A report that can't reach the server is kept and sent automatically for up to a week.</floater.string>
